{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019BPJ2FRyPJDjZnDLMpfgXj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Revamp â€” Description\n2\t\n3\t**North Star:** Make Aurora deliver felt, trustworthy value AND run on a robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture â€” co-equal goals. Success = John sees the reports, can navigate the library, Helping Hand surfaces, he gets a digestible KG summary, trusts the cost numbers, and curation quality (esp. source-quality weighting) + run-robustness improve via the new engine. Substrate: metered API is default (cost bug fixed via thinking_budget=0); flat-rate Claude Max + Gemini Ultra are an optional spike-gated transport, never the foundation; embeddings stay on API. Use the Foreman/Crucible PATTERN (fresh-context sub-agents + adversarial EXECUTEâ†’REVIEWâ†’FIX), NOT its wave-to-done engine. Locked-preserved: KB schema + library, security gating, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n4\t\n5\tCrucible-forged plan (2026-06-06). The adversarial review reframed the original \"rebuild as a Foreman swarm\" ask: ~70% of the felt pain is an unwired consume loop + config bugs, not the discovery engine. Two co-equal tracks â€” close the value loop (visibility, trust, Helping Hand) and build the robust agentic judgment slice (evidence-rigor fix-loop + confidence badge). The parallel judgment fan-out / WAL-actor / durable-checkpoint layer is CUT and tripwired (build only when AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K â‰¥ ~20 AND a measured latency pain); the discovery swarm (scout.fan_out) stays and gains memory in the final wave. Wave 0 (re-light Helping Hand) is already done. See docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md for the full narrative + the deferred-layer rationale.\n6\t\n7\t## Success criteria\n8\t- John sees the morning briefing without opening a folder.\n9\t- The library is navigable (real domain Ã— complexity, not \"(unplaced) ? (?)\").\n10\t- Helping Hand surfaces matches in a Cowork session.\n11\t- Each curation carries a verified/documented/lossy confidence badge (source-quality signal).\n12\t- Cost numbers are trustworthy: every LLM call metered against a matching pricing key.\n13\t- The discovery swarm prioritizes high-yield sources while still exploring new ones.\n14\t- Locked assets (KB schema + library, security gating, cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher) remain intact.\n15\t\n16\t## Provenance\n17\t\n18\tGenerated by Crucible Stage 2 from an approved Master Plan, vetted by the Shark-Tank loop and the well-formedness gate before handoff.\n19\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98d7f83d-ed45-4763-b22e-32416763e6e7","uuid":"b0257d6f-8e9e-4a80-bf70-848691c1cbed","timestamp":"2026-06-13T12:51:01.468Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff\\DESCRIPTION.md","content":"# Aurora Revamp â€” Description\n\n**North Star:** Make Aurora deliver felt, trustworthy value AND run on a robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture â€” co-equal goals. Success = John sees the reports, can navigate the library, Helping Hand surfaces, he gets a digestible KG summary, trusts the cost numbers, and curation quality (esp. source-quality weighting) + run-robustness improve via the new engine. Substrate: metered API is default (cost bug fixed via thinking_budget=0); flat-rate Claude Max + Gemini Ultra are an optional spike-gated transport, never the foundation; embeddings stay on API. Use the Foreman/Crucible PATTERN (fresh-context sub-agents + adversarial EXECUTEâ†’REVIEWâ†’FIX), NOT its wave-to-done engine. Locked-preserved: KB schema + library, security gating, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n\nCrucible-forged plan (2026-06-06). The adversarial review reframed the original \"rebuild as a Foreman swarm\" ask: ~70% of the felt pain is an unwired consume loop + config bugs, not the discovery engine. Two co-equal tracks â€” close the value loop (visibility, trust, Helping Hand) and build th